        <arrangement id="aspace_3e50136c5f6df4a604b3ce961e28469b">
          <head>Arrangement</head>
          <p>Series I is arranged chronologically.</p>
        </arrangement>
        <scopecontent id="aspace_0c0a86773528561dce11a36a4c1bee9f">
          <head>Scope and Contents</head>
          <p>Series I contains correspondence and reports created, received, and/or compiled by Robert Ashe.</p>
          <p>Correspondents include numerous private individuals, many of whom sought Ashe's perspective for their research on humanitarian operations. Representatives of numerous organizations -- government, international, and non-governmental -- are represented in the correspondence as well. This notably includes the militant partisan leader Kong Sileah. Ashe's reports to ICRC and Christian Outreach, circa 1979-1981, feature heavily in this series. Ashe's leadership of Nong Chan, especially regarding the operations of the "Land Bridge," is a central topic across each of these categories.</p>
          <p>Personal narratives written by Cambodian refugees are interspersed across this series. Most of these writings have been translated into English.</p>
        </scopecontent>
