        <arrangement id="aspace_32a14e04f1ca2fc679622ec7160aaceb">
          <head>Arrangement</head>
          <p>Series II is arranged primarily by ascending numerical groupings of film rolls. Within film rolls, files are arranged chronologically.</p>
        </arrangement>
        <processinfo id="aspace_669d4760ed0d3d31e8bdeb19b4d0f997">
          <head>Processing Information</head>
          <p>Photographs were removed from their original housing -- small, flip photo albums -- for preservation considerations during processing. These albums have been retained for their inscriptions and production information and are represented in the description by the file "Original photographic housing, circa 1976-1981."</p>
        </processinfo>
        <scopecontent id="aspace_7f72caabd71fc6dc4fcb662d4723438c">
          <head>Scope and Contents</head>
          <p>Series II contains approximately 1,100 color and black-and-white photographic prints compiled by Robert Ashe. With the exception of one file containing 8"x10" prints, almost all are roughly 3"x5". Versos often contain additional information such as film roll numbers and, ocassionally, descriptive captions.</p>
          <p>Image content features extensive subject matter relating to life in the refugee camps with a focus on Nong Chan. Such content includes though is not limited to images depicting Robert Ashe, resident and non-resident refugees, relief workers, construction of camp facilities, recreational activities, childrens' educational programming, distribution of rice by ICRC, distribution of fishing nets by Christian Outreach, and the funeral of militant partisan leader Kong Sileah.</p>
          <p>Graphic depictions of deceased persons are present in Boxes 3 and 5. These images include depictions of mass graves, decomposing corpses, and victims of the Cambodian Genocide.</p>
        </scopecontent>
